<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Listing 2: </span>System Prompt for Creating Importance Scores</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We also experimented with prompting the LLM to give binary scores <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(c_{i};y^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(c_{i};y^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, rather than floats. The prompt in Listing <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> was used to produce a list of importance scores corresponding to each input sentence as above.</p>
</div>
