<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Direct Abstractive Summarization.</span> We tested the ability of instruction-tuned LLMs to directly create abstractive summaries that retain a specified fraction <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> of important information. To guide the LLM as to what type of information was important for a given dataset, ten examples from the calibration dataset were provided to enable in-context learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
