<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A3.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">User-specified probability of achieving coverage (1-<math id="A3.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>) vs. empirical probability of achieving coverage, on the CNN/DM dataset. Dashed lines show theoretical bounds given in <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Extractive Summarization via Conformal Importance ‣ Document Summarization withConformal Importance Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Results are averaged over 400 random splits of calibration and test data.</span></figcaption>
